3. User Roles and Authentication

Implement secure, role-based authentication and authorization.

A. Super Admin

The Super Admin manages the overall platform.

Required capabilities:

- Secure login.
- Super Admin dashboard.
- Create, activate, deactivate, and manage recruiter accounts.
- View recruiter profiles and account status.
- Assign organizations or companies to recruiters where applicable.
- Manage platform-wide settings.
- Configure interview limits and supported interview configurations.
- View platform-wide analytics.
- Monitor recruitment activity.
- View system usage and interview statistics.
- Manage platform-level permissions.
- Review system errors and operational logs.
- Manage account security and access permissions.

Only authorized Super Admins should have access to these controls.

Public Super Admin registration must not be available. The initial Super Admin account must be created through a secure administrative setup process.

B. Recruiter

Recruiters manage recruitment activities for their assigned organization.

Required capabilities:

- Secure login.
- Recruiter dashboard.
- Create and manage job openings.
- Configure job descriptions and required skills.
- Select the interview process: 5 rounds or 8 rounds.
- Configure AI interviewer settings.
- Generate secure candidate interview links.
- View candidate applications and interview progress.
- Monitor interview completion status.
- Access interview transcripts and recordings when enabled and consented to.
- Review AI-generated interview reports.
- Compare candidates using job-relevant assessment criteria.
- Mark candidates as Shortlisted, On Hold, Rejected, or Selected.
- Manage candidate records.
- View job-wise and candidate-wise analytics.
- Export authorized interview reports.

Recruiters must only access the candidates, jobs, reports, and organization data they are authorized to manage.

C. Candidate

Candidates do not need a recruiter or Super Admin account.

A candidate should enter the interview using a secure invitation link generated for a specific job opening.

Required capabilities:

- Open the invitation link.
- View job details and interview instructions.
- Read the privacy notice and provide required consent.
- Upload a resume in PDF or supported document format.
- Review detected resume information.
- Verify their name, email, and other required details.
- Complete microphone and camera checks.
- Test their internet connection and audio input.
- Start the interview.
- Communicate with the AI interviewer through voice and video.
- View the current interview round and progress.
- Receive appropriate error messages and recovery options.
- Submit the completed interview.
- Receive a confirmation that their interview was submitted.

Candidates must not access recruiter dashboards, internal hiring decisions, other candidates' data, or confidential evaluation notes.

